{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>בדד ממכריו.</b> Some say it is like מאת מכריהם, by a slight stretch, but the grammar does not consent. Rather, it is from the root of וכי תמכרו ממכר. The meaning: if he sold his ancestral house that he inherited from his fathers, as written, ויצא ממכר בית ועיר אחוזתו. This is the interpretation according to the fathers: one may not say to him, 'Here, you have [sold it]; you shall no longer eat,' but he shall eat a portion like a portion. And having completed the mention of the matter of the judge and the priest, he mentioned the matter of the prophet."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The lemma reads לבד ממכריו per the source; Ibn Ezra's discussion treats it as בדד ממכריו (Deut. 18:8 reading בדד rather than לבד)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:53.815077624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}